WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.780
Dear city leaders. Politicians. Decisionmakers.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.260
In the name of all cyclists, I&nbsp;
have an important message for you.
 &nbsp;

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.380
THIS IS NOT BICYCLE INFRASTRUCTURE.&nbsp;

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.680
This is a constant near death&nbsp;
experience for adrenaline junkies.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.820
This is proper bicycle infrastructure. Physically&nbsp;
separated from high speed motor traffic.&nbsp;

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.480
Or this, even. Not as good, but at least&nbsp;
cars don’t have to constantly dodge you.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.730
What, you don’t like fearing for your life when&nbsp;
cars pass you by at high speeds at arm's length?

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.100
Not, not really. I’m weird like that.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.600
As a rule of thumb, if you can’t imagine groups&nbsp;
like pensioners or schoolchildren cycling on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.620
given bike path, it’s a bad bike path. Bike&nbsp;
infrastructure shouldn’t be tailored solely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.000
around fit young adult men in professional biking&nbsp;
gear, who have nothing to fear or nothing to lose.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.500
So here’s what you should be doing. Take a&nbsp;
road. Take one lane, separate it from the rest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.940
and turn it into a dedicated bike lane.&nbsp;
Congratulations! You now have proper bike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.660
infrastructure that people can safely use on&nbsp;
an everyday basis, without the fear of death.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.600
This has been a message from&nbsp;
cyclists to city decision makers.&nbsp;

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.040
Thank you for your kind attention.

